{"judgments": [
 {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The identity of the \"Buyer\" — its name, state of organization and address — and the date of the Agreement are left blank, so the instrument does not on its face show who is bound or when. A court would have to construe whether the assignee developer or GSA is the \"Buyer\" and whether a binding contract was formed at all.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.42}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The \"Property\" is fixed by Exhibit A's legal description and \"approximately 10.89 acres,\" but Section 3 requires a deed containing \"new legal descriptions\" reflecting the vacation of Sixth and Abbott Streets and the contiguous properties thereby created. Whether the vacated street parcels are part of the \"Property\" sold cannot be settled from this clause alone.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This clause conveys Seller's interest in adjoining street beds only \"to the center line thereof,\" while Section 3 contemplates conveyance of the whole contiguous parcels created by vacating Sixth Street and Abbott Street. The two cannot both fix the extent of the street-bed interest conveyed.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"All proper instruments\" for conveyance and for \"the assignment and collection of any such award\" is undefined and unbounded, and the obligation is open-ended in time (\"or thereafter, on demand\"). A court would have to decide what documents Seller can be compelled to sign and for how long.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.14}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
